{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21eb7e39d99b57bc5ab2", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Gravitation - Test 6", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd71"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd6d", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dce9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb0"], "topics": ["60e5678e499d1e49588f927a"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa01b"], "question": {"text": "A body weight <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi></math>, is projected vertically upwards from earth&#39;s surface to reach a height above the earth which is equal to nine times the radius of earth. The weight of the body at that height will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "9867dc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>91</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcea"}, {"id": "7a5777", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dceb"}, {"id": "bc7fba", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcec"}, {"id": "2cf02f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dced"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcee", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb0"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6b"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b2f"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements : one is labelled as Assertion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and the other is labelled as Reason <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>.</p><p>Assertion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;: The escape velocities of planet&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;are same. But <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;are of unequal mass.</p><p>Reason <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>:&nbsp;The product of their mass and radius must be same. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "d30510", "text": "Both&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> are correct and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is the correct explanation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcef"}, {"id": "1b072b", "text": "Both&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;are correct but&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is NOT&nbsp;the correct explanation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcf0"}, {"id": "67929d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is not correct but&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcf1"}, {"id": "a59869", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is correct but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is not correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcf2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcf3", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb0"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f87fd"], "concepts": ["60e56812499d1e49588fa38a"], "question": {"text": "The time period of a satellite, revolving above earth&#39;s surface at a height equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;will be (Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo></math> radius of earth)"}, "options": [{"id": "886bda", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcf4"}, {"id": "bfc5f3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcf5"}, {"id": "b2facc", "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>32</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></msqrt></math></p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcf6"}, {"id": "1b09fd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcf7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcf8", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb0"], "topics": ["6117b60a478ae845c43c63f1"], "concepts": ["6117b607478ae845c43c62fb"], "question": {"text": "Consider a binary star system of star <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and star <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> with masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></math> revolving in a circular orbit of radii <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;respectively. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></math> are the time period of star <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and star <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo></math> respectively, then:"}, "options": [{"id": "3fcd81", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcf9"}, {"id": "d5bea5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcfa"}, {"id": "f18be8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;(if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcfb"}, {"id": "167a19", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>A</mtext></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>B</mtext></msub></math>&nbsp;(if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>A</mtext></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>B</mtext></msub></math>)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcfc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcfd", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb0"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6b"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52bb"], "question": {"text": "Match List I with List II :\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FKWt5Xed_RfsSzcS9jdUnTzchmtngwcH892WlVhodGyw.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "fc312f", "text": "(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcfe"}, {"id": "286f92", "text": "(A)-(II), (B)-(I), (C)-(IV), (D)-(III)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dcff"}, {"id": "1138df", "text": "(A)-(I), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(IV)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd00"}, {"id": "9170e2", "text": "(A)-(I), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(III)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd01"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd02", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb0"], "topics": ["60e5678e499d1e49588f927a"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa01b"], "question": {"text": "The approximate height from the surface of earth at which the weight of the body becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> of its weight on the surface of earth is :<br />[Radius of earth <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>732</mn></math>]"}, "options": [{"id": "7eee98", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3840</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd03"}, {"id": "e5f561", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4685</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd04"}, {"id": "cabc02", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2133</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd05"}, {"id": "aa0bed", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4267</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd06"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd07", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb0"], "topics": ["6117b60a478ae845c43c63f1"], "concepts": ["6117b607478ae845c43c62fb"], "question": {"text": "<p>Assume that the earth is a solid sphere of uniform density and a tunnel is dug along its diameter throughout the earth. It is found that when a particle is released in this tunnel, it executes a simple harmonic motion. The mass of the particle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>. The time period of the motion of the particle will be (approximately)</p><p>(take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>, radius of earth <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "b4e9df", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn></math>&nbsp;hours", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd08"}, {"id": "bb05e2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;hour&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn></math>&nbsp;minutes", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd09"}, {"id": "54d53a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;hour&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn></math>&nbsp;minutes", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd0a"}, {"id": "c5f6f4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math>&nbsp;hours", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd0b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd0c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb0"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6b"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b2f"], "question": {"text": "The mass of the moon is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>144</mn></mfrac></math> times the mass of a planet and its diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math> times the diameter of a planet. If the escape velocity on the planet is v, the escape velocity on the moon will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "6b70c5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd0d"}, {"id": "99cf43", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd0e"}, {"id": "5e7609", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd0f"}, {"id": "4ea3a8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd10"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd11", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb0"], "topics": ["60e5678e499d1e49588f927a"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa01b"], "question": {"text": "An object is taken to a height above the surface of earth at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>R</mi></math> from the centre of the earth. Where radius of earth, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>. The percentage decrease in the weight of the object will be"}, "options": [{"id": "73fe2a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn><mo>%</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd12"}, {"id": "a20baf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd13"}, {"id": "d6cbcf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>64</mn><mo>%</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd14"}, {"id": "94c9fd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>%</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd15"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd16", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb0"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b6b"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52bb"], "question": {"text": "A mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is placed at the center of a uniform spherical shell of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. If the gravitational potential at a point, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> from the center is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> is:"}, "options": [{"id": "360c3c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>G</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8f2ee0e063d929dd17"}, {"id": "b65d64", "text": "<math xmlns=\